{"study_accession":"PRJNA824711","secondary_study_accession":"SRP368223","title":"Transcriptome profiling of 13 HIV positive individuals of variable disease progression from an Indian Cohort","description":"In our cohort study for HIV, we have classified patients in 3 different groups, primarily on the basis latency period- Long term non-progressors (LTNP), Long term non-progressors NON-controllers (LNC), and regular progressors. individuals in these groups differ phenotypically as well as have significantly different levels of CD4+T cell counts and viral loads. Goal of the study is to explore the underlying novel mechanisms behind the differences in different patient classes of HIV using Next-Generation sequencing. Overall design: Transcriptome profiling of three different patient classes of HIV. [contributor] YRGCare, Chennai","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":12,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN27412967","study_accession":"PRJNA824711","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"P68","description":"P68","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM6034520","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-01-01","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["patient class","Regular"],["viral load","155060"],["age","33"],["sex","female"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR18684834","experiment_accession":"SRX14785990","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":29128973,"base_count":5825794600,"first_public":"2023-01-01","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM6034520: P68 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN27412968","study_accession":"PRJNA824711","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"P66","description":"P66","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM6034519","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-01-01","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["patient class